# Rules

One markdown file per rule, nested however you like:

    rules/<rule-name>.md
    rules/<category>/<rule-name>.md

Claude Code loads everything under `~/.claude/rules` as user-scope memory in
every session, walking the tree recursively. A `paths:` frontmatter key narrows
a rule to sessions that touch matching files.

Only `.md` is picked up, and every `.md` found becomes a rule -- which is why
this file carries no extension.

Nothing installs these yet -- the `skills` CLI covers skills only. Copy or
symlink what you want into `~/.claude/rules/` by hand.
